WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.760
Speaker 1: All right. Let's talk about an&nbsp;
incredible story that's both incredible for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:10.400
what it contains, but also because of some of the&nbsp;
reaction that we've seen from some. The Pentagon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:16.880
has admitted to killing 10 civilians, including&nbsp;
up to seven children in a Kabul drone strike&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:22.800
last month. This particular drone strike was&nbsp;
the center of much controversy because it tied&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:27.680
in with the withdrawal from Afghanistan that&nbsp;
Donald Trump initially said he wanted to do,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:34.720
wasn't able to do, and Joe Biden ultimately&nbsp;
did. We now have video of a CENTCOM commander,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:40.640
General Kenneth Mackenzie, saying we&nbsp;
didn't get terrorists, we got civilians.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:48.160
The U.S. is considering reparation payments to&nbsp;
surviving family members. The Pentagon originally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.160 --> 00:00:54.160
said the strike killed two ISIS fighters believed&nbsp;
to be involved in planning attacks against U.S.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.160 --> 00:01:02.160
forces in Kabul. The drone strike came after a&nbsp;
suicide bomb attack by ISIS KIA that resulted in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:10.080
the deaths of 13 U.S. service members and dozens&nbsp;
of Afghans near Kabul's airport. So we're going to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:16.880
look at video of General Kenneth Mackenzie saying,&nbsp;
I apologize for this. And then there's a few&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.880 --> 00:01:22.000
different things that I want to talk about. But&nbsp;
to go into it, to kind of frame this, the reason&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:27.600
this particular drone strike is getting so much&nbsp;
attention is the context in the withdrawal from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:35.760
Afghanistan as retaliation to the ISIS suicide&nbsp;
bombing near the airport that left 13 service&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:41.040
members and more civilians dead. Let's listen.
Speaker 2: I am now convinced that as many as 10&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:45.520
civilians, including up to seven children,&nbsp;
were tragically killed in that strike.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.480 --> 00:01:52.240
Moreover, we now assess that it is unlikely that&nbsp;
the vehicle and those who died were associated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.240 --> 00:01:56.160
with ISIS or were a direct threat to U.S. forces
Speaker 1: so far&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.800 --> 00:02:02.240
killed civilians didn't kill ISIS.
Speaker 2: OK, I offer my profound&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.240 --> 00:02:08.320
condolences to the family and friends of those who&nbsp;
were killed. This strike was taken and the earnest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.320 --> 00:02:14.320
belief that it would prevent an imminent threat to&nbsp;
our forces and the evacuees at the airport. But it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:21.360
was a mistake. And I offer my sincere apology as&nbsp;
the combatant commander, I am fully responsible&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:27.360
for this strike and this tragic outcome.
Speaker 1: So it seems. Incongruous&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.240 --> 00:02:34.640
to be talking about a strike which was supposed&nbsp;
to get ISIS okay, but got 10 civilians,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.640 --> 00:02:40.880
including seven children and saying, I'm sorry,&nbsp;
guys, sorry we didn't get the terrorists, we got&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.880 --> 00:02:45.360
10 civilians. And I get that it's completely&nbsp;
incongruous. It's like visually shocking.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:49.840
Am I really hearing this? Is this how they're&nbsp;
talking about it? This happens all the time.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.720 --> 00:02:56.560
This particular drone strike got more attention&nbsp;
because of the circumstances surrounding it. We've&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.560 --> 00:03:01.760
been talking about the issue of drone strikes&nbsp;
killing civilians for a decade. I mean, we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:06.560
started really talking about it in earnest under&nbsp;
Barack Obama. The drone program under the Obama&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.560 --> 00:03:11.040
administration was one of the biggest foreign&nbsp;
policy criticisms of the Obama administration.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:14.800
Genk Yuga, our friend from the Young Turks,&nbsp;
had a nice series of tweets about pointing to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.440 --> 00:03:22.400
this outrage. It may or may not be real. The&nbsp;
media outrage in response to this admission&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:27.760
from the from the CENTCOM commander. But it's&nbsp;
actually another data point of the media being&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.760 --> 00:03:32.640
against the Afghanistan withdrawal. Genk explains&nbsp;
it. Let's look at these tweets Genk wrote, quote,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:36.960
All the reporters who are outraged by&nbsp;
Pentagon drone strike that killed civilians.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.960 --> 00:03:41.520
Are you guys not aware that we've been killing&nbsp;
civilians with drone strikes for decades?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:47.360
How is this news to you that you are all of a&nbsp;
sudden bothered by it because almost none of you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:54.160
objected before going on to say, interestingly,&nbsp;
this outrage comes as a continuation of corporate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.160 --> 00:03:59.280
media rage over the withdrawal from a war.&nbsp;
This outrage did not at all exist in the middle&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:05.600
of those wars, but now, quote, Reporters are&nbsp;
pissed that the Pentagon makes mistakes. Please,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:11.520
Jenckes is spot on here. It is great that&nbsp;
the Pentagon has taken responsibility for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:15.920
something horrifying. OK, it's great that they're&nbsp;
considering payments, payments, which, of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.920 --> 00:04:19.600
don't bring family back. But what else can&nbsp;
you do now other than get throw money at a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.600 --> 00:04:26.320
problem? Right. But this isn't new and there is&nbsp;
a very cynical nature to this. And it's analogous&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.320 --> 00:04:30.320
to the media reaction to the withdrawal from&nbsp;
Afghanistan. As I've said before, the withdrawal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.320 --> 00:04:35.840
was 100 percent the right thing to do. Had Trump&nbsp;
done, it would have been extremely complicated.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.400 --> 00:04:39.760
Similar things would have happened.&nbsp;
Biden did. It got us out of a war.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.760 --> 00:04:46.560
There has been more criticism from the media,&nbsp;
corporate, centrist media and right wing media&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.560 --> 00:04:51.520
and even left wing media to some degree of Biden&nbsp;
getting out. There's been more scrutiny of Biden&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:55.760
getting out than there was of the 20 years&nbsp;
that we spent there. And in the same way,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.760 --> 00:05:02.320
it's not that this drone strike is irrelevant.&nbsp;
It's it's horrifying. It's a tragedy. It's should&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.320 --> 00:05:07.040
it be criminal, right? I mean, OK, there's no&nbsp;
mitigation about this particular drone strike,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.600 --> 00:05:12.320
but it's being used by some in the media&nbsp;
to further reinforce the idea that leaving&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.320 --> 00:05:18.320
Afghanistan was a mistake when if they cared about&nbsp;
drone strikes, they could have been covering the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.320 --> 00:05:22.720
drone war for the last decade differently&nbsp;
than they did. And they haven't been doing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.720 --> 00:05:28.560
it. And so it's hard to take it all seriously.&nbsp;
Good for Genk for pointing this out. Good that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.560 --> 00:05:33.840
they took responsibility on video in this way.&nbsp;
But this is not a new thing that doesn't change&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.840 --> 00:05:38.240
the seriousness of this particular drone strike.&nbsp;
But we've got to understand this in context and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.240 --> 00:05:42.800
understand the way in which it's useful to the&nbsp;
people that are reporting on it in certain ways

